  "question": {
    "text": "If a right circular cone, having maximum volume, is inscribed in a sphere of radius&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi></math>, then the curved surface area (in <math><msup><mrow><mi>cm</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>) of this cone is :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>8</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>π</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>6</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>π</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>8</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>π</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>6</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>π</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0201_a7b0e8410bf5.png\" style=\"width: 233px; height: 250px;\" /></p><p>In&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#9651;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>M</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>M</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>&#952;</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>h</mi></math>&nbsp;where,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>&nbsp;is radius and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi></math>&nbsp;is height of cone</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>(since, radius of cone <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>M</mi></math>&nbsp;and height of cone <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><mi>C</mi></math>)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#960;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>36</mn><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mo>&#8757;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><mi>cos</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cos</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>72</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi></math></p><p>Differentiating both sides with respect to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi></math>, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>72</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>For maximum value,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>72</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>tan</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Thus, volume is maximum&nbsp;when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>tan</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p>Hence, curved surface area <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>r</mi><msqrt><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>cos</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mo>&#8757;</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>&#960;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfenced><msqrt><mn>36</mn><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>36</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>.</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>24</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>&#960;</mi></math></p>"
  }
}